  "title": "Jansen linkage leg",
  "summary": "a walking leg from your hip height, cut sheet and rod list",
  "description": "Theo Jansen's walking linkage scaled to the hip height you ask: drag the crank and the leg walks along its drawn foot path. Laser-cut birch bars and walnut triangles on brass rod pins, one leg or a pair half a turn apart.",
  "domain": "Mechanisms, laser cutting",
  "process": "Laser cutting of birch and walnut plywood; brass rod pins cut to length, glued in one part each, with DIN 125 washers",
  "tier": "complex",
  "difficulty": {
    "score": 7,
    "rationale": "Closed-form kinematics and searches in formulas, formula-curve sweeps, a five-layer multi-body stack with coupled ranges and measured clearances, and a pair option that changes the structure."
  },
  "standards": [
    "Theo Jansen's link lengths (the \"holy numbers\"), as tabled in Wikipedia's Jansen's linkage and in J. Wang, arXiv:2606.22129, Table 1 (topology from its equations 1 to 3)",
